Ladybird exposes width and stretch on FontFace as two names for the same
descriptor. The constructor prefers width when both names are present.

Blink uses hasWidth() to select the constructor descriptor and maps both
attributes to FontFace::stretch(). Chrome 158.0.8127.37 accepted width
in the constructor and reflected changes through both getters.

WebKit 26.5 reflected writes through both names, but ignored width in
the constructor. Its getter is FontFace::width(). Firefox 151.0 exposed
only stretch. The Gecko source checkout has since added width to
FontFaceImpl::SetDescriptors(), where width takes precedence.
